From feb53aea1f0127bfe179f6b5d31d6cc46f33e808 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 18:29:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0076 -- S3 ViRGE/DX SDAC false-fail VGA-detect
 fallback (additive)

The same doskutsu.exe that boots on the g2k Cirrus CL-GD5430 fails on the
swapped-in S3 ViRGE/DX (86C375) with SDL_Init "No available video device".

Root cause (verified from source + real-HW log): DOSVESA_CreateDevice ->
DOSVESA_SupportsVESA -> DetectVGA writes 0xA5 to the DAC pixel-mask
register (port 0x3C6) and reads it back. On the S3 internal SDAC, 0x3C6
overlays a hidden DAC command register reached via consecutive 0x3C6
reads, so once the SDAC read counter is advanced the readback is not 0xA5.
DetectVGA wrongly concludes "no VGA", SupportsVESA returns false, and
CreateDevice returns NULL. The Cirrus round-trips 0x3C6 cleanly, which is
why the identical binary worked there. MEMBW/HWINV probes pass on the S3
because they bypass SDL's DAC probe (HWINV: VBE 3.0 + 320x240x8 LFB modes,
LFB at 0x78000000; MEMBW set a VBE LFB mode and wrote to it).

Fix is purely additive and runs ONLY when DetectVGA() returns false:
  1. Touch the PEL write-index (0x3C8) to reset the SDAC hidden-command
     read counter, then retry the same 0x3C6 round-trip.
  2. If that still fails, fall back to a VBE controller-info query
     (function 0x4F00 "VESA" signature via GetVESAInfo). A card that
     answers VESA is a usable graphics device regardless of the 0x3C6
     quirk, so treat it as supported instead of returning NULL.
  3. If neither succeeds, return the original "No VGA card detected"
     error (EGA/CGA with no VESA BIOS still correctly rejected).

DetectVGA() and the DetectVGA()==true success path are unchanged
(byte-identical), so Cirrus / Mach64 / plain-VGA behavior is preserved by
construction. Each fallback path logs an "s3-vga-detect" line to
SDLDBG.LOG; a clean pass logs nothing new (inferred by absence). No new
env var or hint.
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosmodes.c | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 69 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosmodes.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosmodes.c
index c734f8964..904e0984e 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosmodes.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosmodes.c
@@ -355,7 +355,76 @@ bool DOSVESA_SupportsVESA(void)
     // We need at least VGA hardware (for mode 13h). EGA and CGA cards
     // do not support 256 colors or programmable palettes.
     if (!DetectVGA()) {
+        // === DOSKUTSU patch SDL/0076 (s3-virge-perf): additive S3
+        // ViRGE/DX SDAC false-fail fallback ==========================
+        //
+        // This whole block runs ONLY when the byte-identical upstream
+        // DetectVGA() 0x3C6 DAC pixel-mask round-trip returns false.
+        // Cirrus / Mach64 / plain VGA pass DetectVGA() and never reach
+        // here, so their detection -> CreateDevice path is unchanged.
+        // (DetectVGA() itself is untouched; the success fall-through at
+        // the bottom of this function is verbatim upstream.)
+        //
+        // Why DetectVGA() FALSE-fails on the S3 ViRGE/DX: its internal
+        // SDAC overlays a hidden DAC command register on port 0x3C6,
+        // reached via consecutive 0x3C6 reads. Once the SDAC's internal
+        // read counter is advanced, a 0x3C6 access lands on the hidden
+        // command register instead of the pixel-mask register, so
+        // writing 0xA5 and reading back does not return 0xA5 -> upstream
+        // wrongly concludes "no VGA" and DOSVESA_CreateDevice returns
+        // NULL -> SDL_Init fails with "No available video device". The
+        // MEMBW / HWINV probes work on the same card because they bypass
+        // this DAC probe entirely (HWINV confirms VBE 3.0 + 320x240x8
+        // LFB modes, LFB at 0x78000000; MEMBW set a VBE LFB mode and
+        // wrote to it). The card is fully usable; only this probe lies.
+        //
+        // NOTE: the "clean pass" case (DetectVGA() == true) is left
+        // log-silent on purpose so the success path stays byte-identical
+        // -- it is still distinguishable in SDLDBG.LOG by the presence of
+        // the GetVESAInfo "DOSVESA-CTRL" lines together with the ABSENCE
+        // of any "s3-vga-detect" line below.
+
+        // Attempt 1: reset the SDAC hidden-command read index by touching
+        // the PEL write-index register (0x3C8), then redo the exact same
+        // 0x3C6 round-trip DetectVGA() does. On the S3 SDAC this resets
+        // the consecutive-0x3C6 read counter so the next 0x3C6 access
+        // hits the real pixel-mask register. If it now round-trips, the
+        // card is a usable VGA whose DAC index was merely mis-positioned.
+        {
+            outportb(VGA_DAC_WRITE_INDEX, 0x00); // reset SDAC read counter
+            (void)inportb(0x80);                 // small I/O delay
+            const Uint8 original = inportb(VGA_DAC_PIXEL_MASK);
+            outportb(VGA_DAC_PIXEL_MASK, 0xA5);
+            (void)inportb(0x80); // small I/O delay
+            const Uint8 readback = inportb(VGA_DAC_PIXEL_MASK);
+            outportb(VGA_DAC_PIXEL_MASK, original);
+            if (readback == 0xA5) {
+                DOSKUTSU_MODES_LOG("s3-vga-detect: 0x3C6 round-trip passed after "
+                                   "SDAC read-index reset (0x3C8 touch) -> usable VGA");
+                (void)GetVESAInfo(); // cache VESA info (matches success path)
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
+
+        // Attempt 2: VBE controller-info fallback. If the BIOS answers
+        // VBE function 0x4F00 with the "VESA" signature (GetVESAInfo()
+        // returns non-NULL), the card is a usable VESA graphics device
+        // regardless of the 0x3C6 quirk. This is exactly the S3 ViRGE/DX
+        // case. Treating it as usable lets DOSVESA_GetDisplayModes
+        // enumerate its VBE LFB modes and the engine run normally.
+        if (GetVESAInfo() != NULL) {
+            DOSKUTSU_MODES_LOG("s3-vga-detect: 0x3C6 round-trip failed (incl. after "
+                               "SDAC reset) but VBE 0x4F00 returned VESA signature "
+                               "-> treating as usable graphics device (VBE fallback)");
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        // Neither path proved a usable device: genuinely no VGA/VESA
+        // (e.g. EGA/CGA with no VESA BIOS). Preserve upstream behavior.
+        DOSKUTSU_MODES_LOG("s3-vga-detect: 0x3C6 round-trip failed AND no VBE "
+                           "controller info -> no usable video device");
         return SDL_SetError("No VGA card detected");
+        // === end patch SDL/0076 fallback ===========================
     }
 
     // Cache VESA info if available (NULL mean we only have VGA).
-- 
2.47.3

